he United States and the United Kingdom. The company sells new and used cars and light trucks through its dealerships and digital platform; and service and insurance contracts. It also engages in the wholesale of used vehicles at third-party auctions; wholesale and retail of vehicle and replacement parts; and arrangement of related vehicle financing. In addition, the company offers automotive maintenance and collision repair services. Group 1 Automotive, Inc. was incorporated in 1995 and is headquartered in Houston, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Daryl Adam Kenningham | CEO, President & Director | Age 61 | Compensation: $3.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 20K people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers, improving at 10%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $21K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Group 1 Automotive, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $3.1B market cap on $22.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +12% over the past three years and +8% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 17% against a 8% cost of capital, a 9-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, and 15% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $424M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 2 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.14\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 18.6% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 2.4% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (17.4% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 75% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 24% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Insiders are net buyers (98% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $210.8M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","16 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Earnings Growth Might Change The Case For Investing In Group 1 Automotive Stock (GPI)","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/retail/nyse-gpi/group-1-automotive/news/earnings-growth-might-change-the-case-for-investing-in-group","date":"2026-11-01","timestamp":1793543650.527,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.718,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"What Is Putting Group 1 Automotive (GPI) Back In The Spotlight?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/retail/nyse-gpi/group-1-automotive/news/what-is-putting-group-1-automotive-gpi-back-in-the-spotlight","date":"2026-10-31","timestamp":1793429126.951,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.743,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Group 1 Automotive (NYSE:GPI) Director Sells $143,286.00 in Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/30/group-1-automotive-nysegpi-director-sells-143286-00-in-stock.html","date":"2026-10-30","timestamp":1793394586.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.9,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"The Technical Signals Behind (GPI) That Institutions Follow","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/52/The_Technical_Sign